# Git and Validation

## Pre-commit / pre-push hooks

- **Pre-push (Husky):** `.husky/pre-push` runs `npm test` (`vitest run --maxWorkers=1`, same as CI). Wired by `prepare` on `npm install`. Bypass with `git push --no-verify` when needed. This does **not** replace GitHub Deploy gating.
- **FAQ (optional pre-commit):** [scripts/pre-commit-faq-check.sh](scripts/pre-commit-faq-check.sh). Install as per comments in the script; separate from Husky.

## Commit Messages

GitHub sync uses `[Author: X] Message` for direct commits; auto-sync MCP writes use `[Author: agent-label] [Auto-sync] staff@email updated files` (staff email stays for token resolution). Set `MCP_AGENT_MODEL` (e.g. `claude-4-sonnet`) so agent commits show `[Author: claude]`.

## Site content (`site_*`) — exception to “ask before commit”

Edits under `site_*/` must be pushed to the **content** GitHub repo in the **same task** (SHA required). That is a standing authorization; do **not** wait for the user to ask, and do **not** confuse this with app-repo commits. See [`site-content-github.mdc`](site-content-github.mdc).

## Validation

Run `scripts/validation` (CLI or service) when changing content or schemas. Fix validation errors before committing.

Pipeline SQLite (events / leases / `pipeline_state`): see [`pipeline-sqlite-migrations.mdc`](pipeline-sqlite-migrations.mdc) — add numbered migrations + `npm run ensure:pipeline-db -- --dry-run` before merge.
